41","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"For knowledge-intensive generation, we experiment with MS-MARCO [1] and Jeopardy question generation, and we ﬁnd that our models generate responses that are more factual, speciﬁc, and diverse than a BART baseline."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_6c09d8a99edf7cbd","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":12,"quote":"f RAG models empha- size three primary quality scores and four essential abilities, which collectively inform the evaluation of the two principal targets of the RAG model: retrieval and generation."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_9045661c1f5ab88c","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"(Left) Naive RAG mainly consists of three parts: indexing, retrieval and generation."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_5a8ae7af32a9d1fc","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"Generation Difficulties. In generating responses, the model may face the issue of hallucination, where it produces con- tent not supported by the retrieved context."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_589bc4e8cae01e02","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":2,"quote":"Section IV concentrates on post- retrieval process and LLM fine-tuning in generation."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_0e9bf113f0bf8d95","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":3,"quote":"In addition, reflection tokens in SELF-RAG enable controllable generation at inference, while RLHF focuses on human preference alignment during training."}